---
import LabShell from '../../../components/scientific-systems/LabShell.astro';
import LabCard from '../../../components/scientific-systems/LabCard.astro';
import RecordedLu from '../../../components/scientific-systems/RecordedLu.astro';
import { labProjects } from '../../../data/scientific-systems';
---
<LabShell title="Scientific Systems Lab" description="Independent numerical and symbolic engines, traceable binary investigations, and reproducible scientific validation.">
  <section class="lab-hero">
    <div><p class="lab-kicker">RESEARCH NOTEBOOK / C++20 SYSTEMS</p><h1>Scientific<br />Systems Lab.</h1><p class="lab-lead">Understand the machinery.<br />Build the mathematics. Test the result.</p><p>Independent engines for scientific computation, with a clear line from evidence to implementation. Two active projects. Five carefully scoped research plans.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="#engines">Explore the engines ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="#method">How the work is validated ↗</a></div></div>
    <div class="lab-hero-art" role="group" aria-label="Current investigation: LU factorization and solving"><p>CURRENT INVESTIGATION / 01</p><div class="lab-equation">PA = LU<br /><small>AX = B → X</small></div><p>FACTOR ONCE. SOLVE MULTIPLE SYSTEMS.</p><div class="lab-snapshot"><div><strong>21</strong><span>numerical test entries</span></div><div><strong>366</strong><span>symbolic reference cases</span></div></div></div>
  </section>
  <div class="lab-topics"><span>C++20 / CMAKE</span><span>EXACT ARITHMETIC</span><span>REA + GHIDRA</span><span>INDEPENDENT REFERENCES</span><span>UPDATED 26 OCT 2026</span></div>
  <section id="engines" class="scientific-section"><div class="scientific-section-heading"><div><p class="lab-kicker">SEVEN QUESTIONS. INDEPENDENT ENGINES.</p><h2>A lab built one subsystem at a time.</h2></div><p>“In progress” identifies working, bounded functionality. “Planning” means implementation has not begun.</p></div><div class="lab-grid">{labProjects.map(project => <LabCard project={project} />)}</div></section>
  <RecordedLu />
  <section id="method" class="scientific-section lab-two-column"><div><p class="lab-kicker">METHOD / EVIDENCE BEFORE CLAIMS</p><h2>Make every result inspectable.</h2><ol class="lab-method"><li><div><strong>Investigate</strong><p>Bind binary observations to hashes, addresses and retained REA records.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>Implement</strong><p>Define a small API and distinguish recovered behavior from new design.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>Validate</strong><p>Use exact identities, residuals, domain tests and independent mathematical references.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>Measure and document</strong><p>Record the environment, samples, limitations and unverified behavior.</p></div></li></ol></div><div class="lab-architecture"><p class="lab-kicker">SELECTIVE REUSE / PLANNED CONNECTIONS</p><h2>Shared contracts.<br />Separate engines.</h2><div class="lab-flow"><span>Numerical</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Circuit simulation</span></div><div class="lab-flow"><span>Symbolic</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Vision math</span><span>Typesetting</span></div><p>These integration edges are planned. Each engine owns its build, tests and documented limits. The portfolio presents results without becoming the computational engine.</p><p class="lab-note">No proprietary cloud algorithms are claimed. Original-DLL numerical equivalence has not been demonstrated.</p></div></section>
  <section class="scientific-section"><p class="lab-kicker">NEXT RESEARCH MILESTONE</p><h2>From linear solves to orthogonal factorizations.</h2><p>Householder QR is the next numerical milestone. Symbolic work will deepen domain-aware validation and transformation traces before adding broader algebra. No repositories have been published for either engine yet.</p><a class="text-link" href="/labs/scientific-systems/numerical/">Read the numerical evidence and measured results ↗</a></section>
</LabShell>
